  "change": "Add a conservative byte-preserving three-way merge for disjoint same-count line edits. VaultStore compares editor base/local bytes with the current file revision, writes only a safe merged result through the existing expected-revision journal, and retains complete incoming and current versions with explicit conflict state when merging is unsafe or the file was deleted.",
  "focused_tests": {
    "command": "cargo test --workspace --locked",
    "names": [
      "merge::tests::combines_disjoint_edits_and_preserves_each_line_ending",
      "merge::tests::recognizes_unchanged_sides_without_normalizing_bytes",
      "merge::tests::rejects_binary_and_invalid_utf8_when_versions_diverge",
      "merge::tests::reports_overlapping_and_structural_edits_without_guessing",
      "tests::sync_revision_merge_fixture_merges_safe_edits_and_preserves_conflicts"
    ],
    "result": "All listed tests and the workspace test command passed on Ubuntu, macOS, and Windows GitHub Actions jobs.",
    "logs": {
      "ubuntu_job_id": 114109290732,
      "macos_job_id": 114109290614,
      "windows_job_id": 114109290796
    }
  },
  "scenario_result": [
    "Disjoint edits to separate existing lines merge while preserving each source line ending, including mixed LF/CRLF/CR input and a UTF-8 BOM.",
    "Identical or unchanged sides are recognized without normalizing bytes.",
    "Overlapping edits, insertions/deletions that shift structure, divergent binary data, and invalid UTF-8 are reported as conflicts rather than guessed into a result.",
    "Conflicts preserve the complete incoming version in protected conflict history and retain the current file; external deletion is not silently resurrected.",
    "The fixture fixtures/sync-revision-merge.json is included in the source inventory with SHA-256 2f1779df40afb673192dd3a683257aa002196c48f562ae599ef5c3a43411f736."
